From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lukaszsobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:36:46 +0200
Subject: drivers: remoteproc: drop the redundant C906L remove callback

devm_rproc_add() already registers devm_rproc_remove(), which calls
rproc_del() when the device is unbound. The driver's .remove callback
called rproc_del() as well, so unloading the module or unbinding the
device deleted the rproc twice: the second call runs list_del_rcu() on
a list node that is already gone and device_del() on a device that is
already deleted.

Drop the .remove callback and let devres do the teardown. The release
order stays correct: devres runs in reverse, so the rproc is deleted,
and the core stopped through its reset line, before the reset control
and the rproc allocation are released, since both were acquired earlier
in probe. platform_set_drvdata() only existed to feed .remove, so it
goes too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/sophgo_cv1800b_c906l.c | 10 ----------
 1 file changed, 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/sophgo_cv1800b_c906l.c b/drivers/remoteproc/sophgo_cv1800b_c906l.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/sophgo_cv1800b_c906l.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/sophgo_cv1800b_c906l.c
@@ -205,8 +205,6 @@ static int cv1800b_c906l_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	// the first call to start() will always fail
 	reset_control_assert(priv->reset);
 
-	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, rproc);
-
 	ret = devm_rproc_add(dev, rproc);
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "rproc_add failed\n");
@@ -214,13 +212,6 @@ static int cv1800b_c906l_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static void cv1800b_c906l_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
-{
-	struct rproc *rproc = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
-
-	rproc_del(rproc);
-}
-
 static const struct of_device_id cv1800b_c906l_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "sophgo,cv1800b-c906l" },
 	{ /* sentinel */ },
@@ -229,7 +220,6 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, cv1800b_c906l_of_match);
 
 static struct platform_driver cv1800b_c906l_driver = {
 	.probe = cv1800b_c906l_probe,
-	.remove = cv1800b_c906l_remove,
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "cv1800b-c906l",
 		.of_match_table = cv1800b_c906l_of_match,
